# Line endings are normalised, in both directions.
#
# Every text file is stored in the repository with LF and checked out with LF,
# on Windows as well as Linux. `text=auto eol=lf` does both halves: `text=auto`
# converts on the way in, `eol=lf` pins the working copy on the way out, which
# means it does not matter what any one contributor has `core.autocrlf` set to.
#
# Two reasons this is not cosmetic. A file committed with CRLF shows up as every
# line changed, which buries a two-line fix in a 400-line diff and makes review
# useless. And this project addresses content by SHA-256 — the same text file
# checked out with CRLF hashes differently from the LF original, so a mixed-ending
# checkout could produce a different object hash for identical content.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Binaries: never touched, never diffed as text.
*.png    binary
*.jpg    binary
*.jpeg   binary
*.gif    binary
*.ico    binary
*.pdf    binary
*.pptx   binary
*.woff   binary
*.woff2  binary
*.ttf    binary
*.otf    binary
*.safetensors binary
*.bin    binary
*.pt     binary
*.pyc    binary
*.zip    binary
